// ============================================================================
// THORDIS.UNK - Lost Vale restoration patched copy (lv-patched tier)
//
// Byte-copy of "shared/data/lv-usecode/UNK files/UNK/THORDIS.UNK" (the
// recovered 1994 snapshot the build already compiled) plus the changes
// below. Line numbers refer to the ORIGINAL unpatched file; this header
// shifts everything below it.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. RESTORATION: Thordis's half of the Passage Test aftermath -
//    TESTPLAN.UNK:195-224, the mirror of what lv-patched/ATLI.UNK change 1
//    restored for Atli.
//
//    WHAT WAS LOST. The 1994 sources split quest step 8 across two classes:
//    EggPlantTest::hatch() (PLNTST.UNK) was the map-wired trigger and
//    TypePoisonPlant::use() (TESTPLAN.UNK) was the scene. TESTPLAN branches
//    on thordisToldTest: when THORDIS sent the Avatar to the Test, ATLI is
//    teleported in and speaks; otherwise THORDIS is teleported in and speaks
//    a parallel exchange of her own. lv-patched/PLNTST.UNK merged the scene
//    mechanics into the hatch and dropped BOTH speeches; ATLI's patch
//    restored his, and its own header recorded the remaining asymmetry:
//    "it teleports Thordis in and leaves her silent. The symmetric fix is a
//    lv-patched/THORDIS.UNK doing for her what this file does for Atli."
//    This is that file. Until now, a player who took the Test on Atli's
//    word woke in the test grounds beside a mute elder and was told nothing
//    - not what happened, not that it was poison, and not that Ezrekal is
//    the only place left to go.
//
//    WHERE IT NOW LIVES. Thordis::use(), immediately after enterConvo() and
//    before the ask list is built - the same seam ATLI uses, for the same
//    reasons: they are already HER lines (TESTPLAN's else branch teleports
//    HER in and gives HER this speech), she is standing right beside the
//    Avatar when he wakes, and the exchange is a fixed call-and-response
//    with scripted Avatar lines, so it must play as a scene rather than sit
//    in a menu a player can decline to open. It plays on approach, once.
//
//    HOW IT IS GUARDED. `if (haveMark = true) and (thordisToldTest = false)
//    and (endOfPlantScene = false)`.
//
//      - haveMark is the entry condition, exactly as in ATLI: PLNTST.UNK:186
//        sets it as the scene ends and nothing in the corpus clears it.
//
//      - thordisToldTest = FALSE, not `atliToldTest = true`, and this is a
//        deliberate correction rather than a transcription. TESTPLAN's own
//        comment on the branch reads `else //if atliToldTest = true`, but
//        atliToldTest has **ZERO writers in the entire corpus** - it is
//        declared in FLAGS.UNK, read three times in ATLI and once in
//        EZREKAL, and never once set. A guard keyed on it would be born
//        dead, the same trap decision A hit with avatarPoisoned. The
//        negation is also the STRONGER guard: lv-patched/PLNTST.UNK:83
//        dispatches on `if thordisToldTest = true` and teleports Thordis in
//        on the else, so `thordisToldTest = false` is precisely "Thordis is
//        the elder standing here". It is the exact complement of ATLI's
//        guard, so one and only one of the two blocks can ever fire - which
//        is what makes it safe for both to write the shared latch.
//
//      - endOfPlantScene is the one-shot, shared with ATLI's block. ATLI's
//        header says "do not set it anywhere else"; this block is the one
//        legitimate exception, because it is the same scene's ending on the
//        other branch and the two guards are mutually exclusive.
//
//    IT ALSO ENDS THE SCENE. `plantScene = false` sits beside the latch,
//    mirroring ATLI change 3 site 1: her closing 1994 line is "Leave you
//    alone now I will", and the flag is what was keeping both elders'
//    schedules frozen. With this block in place, the self-heal in
//    Atli::schedule is no longer the mirror path's only release - it is now
//    purely the backstop for a player who never talks to the elder at all.
//
//    MECHANICAL EDITS TO THE CARRIED STATEMENTS - two, both forced by the
//    move, neither touching a string literal:
//      - `Thordis.bark(...)` -> `bark(...)`. TESTPLAN spoke from another
//        class and needed the receiver; inside Thordis's own use() the bare
//        form is this file's convention throughout (cf. line 937 and ~60
//        others). The string literals are byte-identical, including
//        "Gunnar's" - see the spelling note below.
//      - TESTPLAN's closing `Thordis.cSetActivity(ACT_LOITER);` is NOT
//        repeated: exitConvo() reruns Thordis::enterFastArea, which is
//        loiter (u8c_codegen _gen_exit_convo), so it is subsumed rather than
//        dropped.
//    `Avatar.bark(...)` is unchanged. No connecting, bridging or invented
//    line has been added - every spoken word below is 1994 text carried
//    over verbatim from TESTPLAN.UNK:197-222, so the "Elean Speak" inverted
//    word order (speech-patterns.md, decision G) is preserved by
//    construction rather than by imitation. The lines are English-only
//    because TESTPLAN was never translated (its header still reads "@@@
//    READY TO TRANSLATE F & G 8-11-94"); inventing French for them would be
//    fabrication, so they carry no \f/\g markers.
//
//    THE SPELLING. The restored text contains one "Gunnar's" (TESTPLAN:200,
//    "So cruel those Gunnar's are!"). It is carried VERBATIM. The
//    2026-07-19 sweep normalised the clan name to "Gunnars" in RAGNAR and
//    the Zealan spellings in EZREKAL, and this file still holds ten more
//    "Gunnar's" of its own; normalising one restored line while ten
//    neighbours keep the old spelling would be less consistent, not more.
//    The sweep now has a home here and can be done as its own change -
//    noting that three of the ten (lines 459, 1139 and 1141 of the original)
//    are an askList add, its case and its removal, so those three must move
//    together or the option stops matching its own handler.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. line 141: `if (thordisSchedule = at_home)` ->
//    `if (thordisSchedule != in_field)` (2026-10-07).
//    schedule() stores thordisSchedule only after canSafeTeleport, which
//    is deferred (its 1994 destinations predate the rebuilt Map 10), so
//    the global stays 0. With at_home pinned to 1 (retail ARAMINA/SALKIND)
//    and in_field to 2, a 0 matched neither branch and Thordis got no
//    activity at all (verifier finding 1, docs/playtest-2026-10-07-wave1.md).
//    Any value but the field is home, which is what every build before the
//    pins did.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 3. enterFastArea gains `if plantScene = true { return; }` after its
//    inShadeScene guard (2026-10-07), the guard schedule() already has.
//    PLNTST kills her activity and teleports her onto the test grounds;
//    entering the fast area there then spawned a loiter mid-scene, and in
//    one run she walked off the z 64 plateau to z 0 under it (finding 1 of
//    part 2, docs/playtest-2026-10-07-wave1.md). She now stands where the
//    scene put her until the scene-end conversation clears plantScene.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 4. line 971, case "Tell me about the other people.":
//    `spawn toldOthersConvo() -> return;` -> `toldOthersConvo();`
//    (2026-10-07). A `spawn x -> return;` does not wait for x (retail
//    rule c, compiler wave 2), so use() went straight back to its own
//    `answer = ask(askList)` while toldOthersConvo() asked "Your people. /
//    The others.": two ask menus open at once, drawn over each other
//    (A3a, docs/playtest-2026-10-07-wave2-a.md). The plain call spawns
//    the sub-conversation and waits for it (rule a), so its menu is the
//    only one until it returns, as every build before wave 2 played it.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 5. toldOthersConvo: each person block's closing `tempKey = ask(tempList);`
//    is guarded by `if toldMyTribe = false` (You, Tyorvi, Ragnar) or
//    `if toldOthers = false` (Atli, Ingyald, Hrodny, Ezrekal) (2026-10-07).
//    Telling the last person of a group empties tempList, and ask() of an
//    empty list opens a menu with no rows that can never answer. Since
//    change 4 use() waits on this routine, so that left the Avatar frozen
//    for good (docs/playtest-2026-10-07-wave2-final-a.md, finding 1). The
//    routine now returns and use()'s own menu comes back.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// KNOWN GAPS THIS PATCH DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CLOSE (all pre-existing, all
// live-branch re-gates rather than the restoration this change is):
//
//   - **testFromThordis has no writer either.** It is read twice here
//     (original lines 466 and 512) and set nowhere in the corpus, so
//     `not testFromThordis` is permanently true. Two consequences, both on
//     the OTHER path (the one where Thordis sent the Avatar and Atli speaks
//     the aftermath), neither touched here: her case "I have taken your
//     Test." (original line 1443, complete, and the only writer of
//     zealanMark) is unreachable; and every poisoned mark-less player instead
//     gets "Help me, I've been poisoned." / "The Test was impossible!",
//     whose barks blame Atli - "Told you, that rotting pile of fish offal,
//     Atli did!" - even when it was Thordis herself who sent them. The
//     one-token repair is to re-gate both reads onto thordisToldTest, which
//     is written exactly where she tells the Avatar to take the Test
//     (original lines 1213 and 1243).
//     T2 (2026-08-17, PROVISIONAL - review wanted, same status as
//     EZREKAL E5/E6 and TYORVI T1): that repair is now MADE - both reads
//     re-gated `testFromThordis` -> `thordisToldTest` (same token length,
//     no offset shift). It is a live-branch change: the Thordis-sent
//     poisoned player now sees her authored "I have taken your Test."
//     thread (the only zealanMark writer) instead of the Atli-blame
//     thread; the Atli-sent player's routing is unchanged. Verified
//     in-engine 2026-08-17 (part 4 addendum of the day's report).
//
//   - **zealanMark is NOT set by this block**, and that is deliberate. Her
//     restored speech ends "give you the Zealan Mark I will", and 1994 does
//     pair that beat with `zealanMark = true` in the parallel case at
//     original line 1452. But zealanMark is also the discriminator for her
//     whole poisoned ask tree (original line 510): setting it here would
//     route the mirror-path player straight PAST the Atli-blaming follow-up
//     thread that 1994 authored for exactly this player. The Mark itself is
//     granted by the hatch (haveMark), which is the flag the quest reads.
//
//   - atliMet's mirror, thordisMet, is not set by this exchange either -
//     same reasoning as ATLI's patch: writing it would silently re-route
//     this file's own greeting branch.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// S1. lines 104-106 and 111-113 (2026-10-08, Douglas's decision): the
//    schedule() destinations retargeted to the rebuilt Map 10. Both
//    1994 points were pre-rebuild coordinates at z 64 over z-0 ground
//    (docs/playtest-2026-10-07-wave1.md). Slot timing is unchanged;
//    only the x/y/z literals move. In the fields (daytide):
//    (12904,13976,64) -> (5247,9343,0), the Hoskuld farm plots. At home
//    (otherwise): (11052,12724,64) -> (4415,7423,0), in front of the
//    Hoskuld Elder's hut (hut lot 1). METHOD
//    safeTeleport/canSafeTeleport are called for real from the same day
//    (u8c_symbols.METHOD_ROUTINES): retail teleports exactly to the
//    point, checking only that the Avatar is over 700 units from both
//    the NPC and the point, so
//    agents/map-populator/src/test_schedule_destinations.py checks
//    every compiled destination with exact_reach on the built
//    FIXED.DAT.
//    Change 2's "canSafeTeleport, which is deferred" no longer holds,
//    and this is also her way off the z 64 Test plateau: once the scene
//    end clears plantScene, the next scheduler run with the Avatar 700
//    units away sends her to one of these points; when the self-heal
//    clears it (change 6), the same run does.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 6. line 93 (2026-10-10): schedule()'s `if plantScene = true { return; }`
//    becomes the self-heal ATLI change 3 site 2 has: return only while
//    the Avatar is on the Test Grounds plateau, else clear plantScene and
//    go on. SchedulerProcess::run calls schedule() for actor slots 1..255
//    in ascending order, so when only Atli (107) cleared the flag, she
//    (106) had already returned in that pass and stayed on the z 64
//    plateau one more game hour (docs/playtest-2026-10-09-final.md
//    finding 2). Now the first elder to run in the pass ends the scene,
//    and she leaves in the same pass as Atli. The scene-end conversation
//    still clears the flag itself, so that path is unchanged.
//    Test: test_uc_dialogue.py D14c.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 7. lines 1094, 1096, 1103 and 1115 (2026-10-10): the Test chain's menu
//    strings match again. "Tell me of the Test." (line 1084, offered to a
//    met, unpoisoned, unmarked Avatar once testFromAtli is set - Atli's
//    Rite of Passage case writes it) adds "I will take your Test." (line
//    1091) and its case was typed without the period, so the pick matched
//    nothing; the same for the "Yes." / "No." it offers (line 1100), whose
//    cases read "Yes" and "No" while the removals in both (1105, 1117) use
//    the add's text. The case side is changed in all three, 1 byte each:
//    the add and the removals agree. Found by test_uc_dialogue.py D19b.
//    With the case live, the line inside it (1096) re-added its own option
//    with `^=` (the union; every sibling case removes its own option with
//    `-=`), so the answered option stayed on the menu beside "Yes." and
//    "No.": `^=` -> `-=`, 1 byte, found by D19c's walk. ("Not strong
//    enough?" has the same `^=` at line 1128 and is left alone: that case
//    ends the conversation, so nothing is left on screen.)
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 8. line 1439 (2026-10-10): case "I have taken your Test." gains the
//    labels "The plant exploded!" and "What is happening to me?", the two
//    options offered beside it (lines 519-521: poisoned, no Mark, once
//    thordisToldTest is written - T2's live branch). No case had either
//    text, so both picks drew no reply. The case's own removal (1441-1443)
//    already names all three options, which is the author's evidence that
//    its reply ("Poisoned, you have been... Here, the Mark, is.") answers
//    all three. Found by test_uc_dialogue.py D19b's exhaustive scan.
//
// No other byte of the 1994 file is changed.
// ============================================================================

//@@@ READY TO TRANSLATE FRENCH AND GERMAN 7-25
uses "flags";
uses "free";
uses "npc";


npcclass Thordis inherits Npc
{
	process look();
	process use();
	process schedule(currentTime : Long);
	process enterFastArea();
	process leaveFastArea();
	process cast(ref : Referent);
	process randomBarkInField();
	process randomBarkAtHome();
	process toldOthersConvo();
}


process Thordis::look()
{
	if thordisName and thordisJob
	{
		if Thordis.isDead()
		{
			bark("Body of Clan Elder Thordis");
			return;
		}
		else
		{
			bark("Clan Elder Thordis");
			return;
		}
	}

	else if thordisName
	{
		if Thordis.isDead()
		{
			bark("Thordis's lifeless body");
			return;
		}
		else
		{
			bark("Thordis");
			return;
		}
	}

	else if thordisJob
	{
		if Thordis.isDead()
		{
			bark("Clan Elder's lifeless body");
			return;
		}
		else
		{
			bark("Clan Elder");
			return;
		}
	}

	else
	{
		if Thordis.isDead()
		{
			bark("woman's body");
			return;
		}
		else
		{
			bark("woman");
			return;
		}
	}
}


process Thordis::schedule(currentTime:Long)
{
	if Thordis.isDead()
	{
		return;
	}

	if inShadeScene = true
	{
		return;
	}

	// SCENE-END SELF-HEAL (lv-patched change 6), the same test as
	// Atli::schedule's: hold only while the Avatar is on the Test Grounds
	// plateau. She is slot 106 and runs before Atli (107) in each pass.
	if plantScene = true
	{
		if (Avatar.getMap() = MapLostVale)
		and (Avatar.getX() >= 12288) and (Avatar.getX() < 13312)
		and (Avatar.getY() >= 29184) and (Avatar.getY() < 30208)
		{
			return;
		}

		plantScene = false;
	}

	point : WorldPoint;
	map : MapNum = MapLostVale;
	sched : Number;

	if (getPeriod()=daytide)  // IN THE FIELDS
	{
		point.x = 5247;
		point.y = 9343;
		point.z = 0;
		sched = in_field;
	}
	else // AT HOME
	{
		point.x = 4415;
		point.y = 7423;
		point.z = 0;
		sched = at_home;
	}

	if canSafeTeleport(point, MapLostVale)
	{
		thordisSchedule = sched;
		safeTeleport(point, MapLostVale);
	}

}


process Thordis::enterFastArea()
{
	if Thordis.isDead()
	{
		return;
	}

	if inShadeScene = true
	{
		killProcess(referent, PT_ACTIVITY);
		return;
	}

	if plantScene = true
	{
		return;
	}

	resetRef(referent, PT_BARK);

	if (thordisSchedule != in_field)
	{
		cSetActivity(ACT_LOITER);
		spawn randomBarkAtHome() -> return;
	}
	else if (thordisSchedule = in_field)
	{
		cSetActivity(ACT_LOITER);
		spawn randomBarkInField() -> return;
	}
}


process Thordis::leaveFastArea()
{
	killProcess(referent, PT_ACTIVITY);
	resetRef(referent, PT_PATHFIND);
	resetRef(referent, PT_ANIM);
	resetRef(referent, PT_BARK);

	if isDead()
	{
		teleport(urandom(10000), urandom(10000), 0, 0);
	}
}


process Thordis::cast(ref:Referent) // this is for calling the shades
{
	count : Number;
	count = 10;

	while (not getTarget()) and (count)
	{
		wait(1);
		count--;
	}

	ref = getTarget();

	if ref = Avatar:Referent
	{
		spawn callTheShades() -> return;

		if not isDead()
		{
			killProcess(referent, PT_ACTIVITY);
			killProcess(referent, PT_BARK);
			bark("Help! Help! Shades, me, protect!");
		}
	}
}


process Thordis::randomBarkAtHome()
{
	[[PT_ACTIVITY, referent]];

	avaP,torP : WorldPoint;
	ran : Number;

	avaP.x = Avatar.getX();
	avaP.y = Avatar.getY();
	avaP.z = Avatar.getZ();
	torP.x = Thordis.getX();
	torP.y = Thordis.getY();
	torP.z = Thordis.getZ();

	ran = getDistance(avaP, torP);

	if (ran < 200)
	{
		ran = urandom(8);

		if ran = 1
		{
			turnToFace(getDirToItem(Avatar:Referent), false, 10);
			bark("Hello?");
			realDoAnim(AS_FIDGET, getDir());
			wait(120);
		}

		if ran = 2
		{
			turnToFace(getDirToItem(Avatar:Referent), false, 10);
			bark("Need what, do you?");
			realDoAnim(AS_FIDGET, getDir());
			wait(120);
		}

		if ran = 3
		{
			bark("Resting, I am. Away, go.");
			wait(60);
		}

		if ran = 4
		{
			bark("Speak to anyone, wish, I do not!");
			wait(120);
		}
	}
	else
	{
		ran = urandom(12);
		turnToFace(urandom(7),0,10);

		if ran = 1
		{
			bark("Curse Ingyald, the Ancient Ones should!");
			wait(60);
		}

		if ran = 2
		{
			bark("With Tyorvi, do what, can I?");
			realDoAnim(AS_FIDGET,getDir());
			wait(60);
		}

		if ran = 3
		{
			bark("Lonely, I am... The last Elder, shall I be.");
		}

		if ran = 4
		{
			bark("Why Ancient Ones, forsaken us, have you?");
			wait(60);
		}

		if ran = 5
		{
			bark("Do something for my poeple, I must!");
		}

		if ran = 6
		{
			bark("No comfort, the shades offer. No answer, they have.");
		}

		if ran = 7
		{
			bark("Failed, I have. Lost, lost, we are...");
			wait(100);
		}
	}
}


process Thordis::randomBarkInField()
{
	[[PT_ACTIVITY, referent]];

	avaP,torP : WorldPoint;
	ran : Number;

	avaP.x = Avatar.getX();
	avaP.y = Avatar.getY();
	avaP.z = Avatar.getZ();
	torP.x = Thordis.getX();
	torP.y = Thordis.getY();
	torP.z = Thordis.getZ();

	ran = getDistance(avaP, torP);

	if (ran < 200)
	{
		ran = urandom(8);

		if ran = 1
		{
			turnToFace(getDirToItem(Avatar:Referent), false, 10);
			bark("Hello?");
			realDoAnim(AS_FIDGET, getDir());
			wait(120);
		}

		if ran = 2
		{
			turnToFace(getDirToItem(Avatar:Referent), false, 10);
			bark("Upon the plants, step not!");
			realDoAnim(AS_FIDGET, getDir());
			wait(120);
		}

		if ran = 3
		{
			bark("Withering, the poor crops are. More water, need, they do.");
			wait(60);
		}

		if ran = 4
		{
			bark("Poor, our soil is...");
			wait(120);
		}
	}
	else
	{
		ran = urandom(12);
		turnToFace(urandom(7),0,10);

		if ran = 1
		{
			bark("Feed us for long, this will not.");
			wait(60);
		}

		if ran = 2
		{
			bark("At these leaves, look!");
			bark("Eating better than us, the insects are!");
			realDoAnim(AS_FIDGET, getDir());
			wait(60);
		}

		if ran = 3
		{
			bark("Ancient Ones, need more food, we do!");
		}

		if ran = 4
		{
			bark("To haul water, need Tyorvi, I do.");
			wait(60);
		}

		if ran = 5
		{
			bark("Find game soon, I hope Ragnar does.");
			bark("Last long, these crops will not.");
		}

		if ran = 6
		{
			bark("Every year, worse, the crops get.");
		}

		if ran = 7
		{
			bark("Lay down and die, I should. No hope, there is...");
			wait(100);
		}
	}
}


process Thordis::use()
{
	ran : Number;
	ran = urandom(5);

	if not thordisMet
	{
		if ran = 1
		{
			Avatar.bark("Greetings!");
		}
		else if ran = 2
		{
			Avatar.bark("Hail, stranger!");
		}
		else if ran = 3
		{
			Avatar.bark("Good day!");
		}
		else
		{
			Avatar.bark("Well met!");
		}
	}
	else
	{
		if ran = 1
		{
			Avatar.bark("Greetings, Thordis!");
		}
		else if ran = 2
		{
			Avatar.bark("Hail, Thordis!");
		}
		else if ran = 3
		{
			Avatar.bark("Good day, Thordis!");
		}
		else
		{
			Avatar.bark("Well met, Thordis!");
		}
	}

	askList, tempList : String List;
	answer, tempKey : String;

	enterConvo();

	// ---- RESTORATION (lv-patched): the Passage Test aftermath, Thordis's
	// half. TESTPLAN.UNK:195-224, the else branch - her own lines, dropped
	// when lv-patched/PLNTST.UNK merged the scene into the egg hatch. Plays
	// once, on the first conversation after the Test, and only when SHE is
	// the elder the hatch teleported in. See the file header.
	if (haveMark = true) and (thordisToldTest = false)
	and (endOfPlantScene = false)
	{
		bark("Oh my, terrible this is. Send you here Atli did?");

		Avatar.bark("Yes.");

		bark("So cruel those Gunnar's are! Tell you did he
		poisonous the plant is and no antidote there is?");

		Avatar.bark("No!");

		bark("As much I thought. In the days before
		the Great Cataclysm, given to teach our youngsters about
		their own mortality this test was. From the Ancient
		Ones the only antidote was. Now that reach the Ancient
		Ones the High Priestess cannot, afraid you are doomed I am.");

		Avatar.bark("This can not be!");

		bark("Sad to say it I am. But give you the Zealan
		Mark I will. With it recognized as a full Zealan you will be,
		for the short time you have.");

		Avatar.bark("Is there no shred of hope?");

		bark("Well, speak to Ezrekal you can, but afraid I am no good
		it will do. Leave you alone now I will.");

		// The one-shot latch, shared with lv-patched/ATLI.UNK: the two
		// guards are exact complements, so only one block ever writes it.
		endOfPlantScene = true;
		// SCENE END, the mirror of ATLI change 3 site 1: hand both elders
		// their schedules back. "Leave you alone now I will" is Thordis
		// saying this line out loud.
		plantScene = false;
		exitConvo();
		return;
	}


	if not thordisMet
	{
		askList ^= <<"How are you called?",
    				"What is it you do?",
    				"What is this place?">>;
	}
	else // thordisMet
	{
		askList ^= <<"Tell me about the other people.">>;

		if not avatarPoisoned
    	{
        	if not zealanMark
        	{
            	if testFromAtli
            	{
                	askList ^= <<"Can you direct me to the Test?",
                            	"Tell me of the Test.">>;

					if gunnarSpokeStone
					{
						askList ^= <<"The Gunnar's say you have the Stone.">>;
					}
					else
					{
						askList ^= <<"Where is the Passage Stone?">>;
					}
				}
            	else if not thordisToldTest
            	{
                	if tyorviMet or ragnarMet
                	{
                    	askList ^= <<"Why will no one speak to me?">>;
                	}
                	else if atliMet or hrodnyMet or ingyaldMet
                	{
                    	askList ^= <<"Why will no one speak to me?">>;
                	}
                	else
                	{
                    	askList ^= <<"How may I be accepted?">>;
                	}
            	}
            	else
            	{
                	askList ^= <<"Why must I take the Test?",
                        	"What happens if I fail?",
                        	"Where is the Test?",
							"Where is the Passage Stone?">>;
            	}
        	}
        	else // Have Mark, But Not Poisoned
        	{
            	if not templeOpen
            	{
                	askList^= <<"I have returned the shield. Now what?">>;
            	}
            	else
            	{
                	if not godsFree
                	{
                    	askList ^= <<"How do I free the gods?">>;
                	}
                	else
                	{
                    	askList ^= <<"What will happen now?">>;
                	}
            	}
        	}
		}
        else    // Poisoned
        {
           	if not zealanMark
           	{
               	if not thordisToldTest
               	{
                   	askList ^= <<"Help me, I've been poisoned.",
                               	"The Test was impossible!">>;
               	}
               	else  // testFromThordis, but no mark
               	{
                   	askList ^= <<"I have taken your Test.",
                               	"The plant exploded!",
                               	"What is happening to me?">>;
               	}
           	}
           	else    // have mark
            {
               	if not toldCliffs
               	{
                   	if not ezrekalMet
                   	{
                       	askList ^= <<"Can you heal me?">>;
                   	}
                   	else
                   	{
                       	askList ^= <<"Ezrekal can do nothing!",
                                   	"Is there no hope for me?">>;
                   	}
               	}
               	else
               	{
                   	if not climbedCliffs // toldCliffs, but not haveShield
                   	{
						if toldAboutAddiction
						{
                       		askList ^= <<"Tell me more of the cliffs.",
										"What happened to Tyorvi?">>;
						}
						else
						{
                       		askList ^= <<"Tell me more of the cliffs.",
                               		"Has no one climbed the cliffs before?">>;
						}
                   	}
                   	else    // toldCliffs and haveShield
                   	{
                       	// Shade Scene
                   	}
               	}
            }
        }
    }

	while answer != "bye"
	{
		askList -= <<"bye">>;
		askList += <<"bye">>;

		answer = ask(askList);

		switch answer
		{
			case "How are you called?"
			{
				askList -= <<"How are you called?">>;
				bark("Thordis, I am. After my great-grandmother named I was.
					The one to tell me the first tales she was. Though quite
					old she was.");

				if (saidGrandmother = false)
				{
					askList ^= <<"Great-grandmother?", "First tales?">>;
				}
				else
				{
					askList ^= <<"First tales?">>;
				}

				thordisMet = true;
				thordisName = true;
			}

			case "Great-grandmother?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Great-grandmother?">>;
				bark("The term you know not? Different you are. But how
    				different, know I did not. Perhaps, hatched you are...
    				whatever you are.");
				bark("My mother's mother, Thordis was called. Elder she
    				was. As Elder all women of my family have been.");

				saidGrandmother = true;

				if (thordisJob = false) and (saidWomen = false)
				{
    				askList ^= <<"Elder?", "All the women?">>;
				}
				else if (thordisJob = true) and (saidWomen = false)
				{
    				askList ^= <<"All the women?">>;
				}
				else  // if (thordisJob = false) and (saidWomen = true)
				{
					askList ^= <<"Elder?">>;
				}
			}

			case "Elder?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Elder?">>;
				bark("Know such a simple word you do not? In your clan
    				who leads? Speak for all one must, or chaos all will
    				be.");
				bark("Responsible for her people an Elder is. To her,
    				answer they must. And answer to the gods, she must.
    				Act for the good of all she must.");

				thordisJob = true;
				thordisMet = true;
			}

			case "All the women?"
			{
				askList -= <<"All the women?">>;
				bark("Hmmm. Think, I must. Confuses me, talking with you
    				does. Speak like a human you do not.");
				bark("When more than one woman there is, no. If two women
    				there are, to the oldest the job falls. But in a long
    				while, happened that has not.");

				saidWomen = true;

				askList ^= <<"Not like a human?", "In a long while?">>;
			}

			case "Not like a human?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Not like a human?">>;
				bark("No offense I meant. Prefer To be called a Pagan
    				you would?");

				tempList ^= <<"I am not a Pagan.",
	    					"It doesn't matter.">>;

				tempKey = ask(tempList);

				if tempKey = "I am not a Pagan."
				{
    				tempList -= <<"I am not a Pagan.",
			    				"It doesn't matter.">>;
    				bark("Well, obvious it is Zealan you are not.
	    				In fact, the likes of you never seen I have.");
    				bark("What are you?");

    				tempList ^= <<"I am from Earth.",
			    				"I am from Britannia.",
			    				"I am the Avatar.">>;

					tempKey = ask(tempList);

					if tempKey = "I am from Earth."
					{
						tempList -= <<"I am from Earth.",
    								"I am from Britannia.",
    								"I am the Avatar.">>;
						bark("Pagan, you are! A spy from foul Lithos!
    						Liar! Murderer! Be gone!");

						tempList  ^= <<"No, I am from another planet!",
    								"What is Lithos?">>;

						tempKey = ask(tempList);

						if tempKey = "No, I am from another planet!"
						{
          					tempList  -= <<"No, I am from another planet!",
		            					"What is Lithos?">>;
          					bark("Have me belive such a story, you would?
	           					Either crazy you are or fool I am, you
	           					think!");
          					bark("In how you speak and act, Pagan, take care.
	           					Lest the shades of our ancestors I call forth!");

							answer = ask(askList);
						}
						else
						{
          					tempList  -= <<"No, I am from another planet!",
		            					"What is Lithos?">>;
          					bark("Either fool you are, or fool I am, you
	           					think. Your tales know you do not?");
          					bark("Take care! The shades of our ancestors,
	           					ignorant children will take.");

							answer = ask(askList);
						}
					}
					else if tempKey = "I am from Britannia."
					{
        				tempList -= <<"I am from Earth.",
			          				"I am from Britannia.",
          							"I am the Avatar.">>;
        				bark("Answer my question that does not. Know where
         					such a place is I do not. Pagan, still you seem.
         					But to be insulting, wish I do not.");
           				bark("Now what saying, I was?");

						answer = ask(askList);
					}
					else
					{
        				tempList -= <<"I am from Earth.",
			          				"I am from Britannia.",
			          				"I am the Avatar.">>;
        				bark("But " + getName() + " your name is, you said.");
        				bark("Talk to you for so long, I should not. Makes
	         				my head hurt, it does!");
        				bark("Now what saying, I was?");

						answer = ask(askList);
					}
				}
				else
				{
    				tempList -= <<"I am not a Pagan.",
			    				"It doesn't matter.">>;
  					bark("Matter, it should! To be a Pagan called, a foul thing
   						is. Your tales, know, you do not?");
  					bark("Take care! The shades of our ancestors,
   						ignorant children will take.");
  					bark("Now what saying, I was?");

					answer = ask(askList);
				}
			}

			case "In a long while?"
			{
				askList -= <<"In a long while?">>;
				bark("In my memory, more than one child no family has
    				had.");
				bark("Seen our land, you have. Little food, there is.
    				And drying up, our water is.");
				bark("Few children, we have. Which is why, cherish them, we
    				do. And why our history, so tragic is.");

				tempList  ^= <<"Why is the land so barren?",
	        				"Why is your history tragic?">>;
				tempKey = ask(tempList);

				if tempKey = "Why is the land so barren?"
				{
    				askList -= <<"Why is the land so barren?">>;
    				bark("Broken tradition, we have. Turned their backs on
        				us they have. Angry at us, they are.");

    				tempList ^= <<"Broken tradition?",
                				"Why are they angry?">>;

					tempKey = ask(tempList);

	        		if tempKey = "Broken tradition?"
        			{
            			askList -= <<"Broken tradition?">>;
            			bark("To the temple, go, we do not. The shades of our
                			ancestors, at the sacred place, honor, we do not.");
            			bark("As it was, nothing is. Changed, everything has.");

            			tempList ^= <<"Why don't you go to the temple?",
                        			"What are the shades?",
                        			"Why don't you honor your ancestors?",
                        			"Why has everything changed?">>;
            			tempKey = ask(tempList);

            			if tempKey = "Why don't you go to the temple?"
                		{
                    		tempList -= <<"Why don't you go to the temple?">>;
                    		bark("No use in going to the temple, there is.
                        		Sealed, it is. As sealed, it was, in the days
                        		of my great-grandmother.");

                    		tempList ^= <<"Why is the temple sealed?">>;
                		}

                		if tempKey = "Why is the temple sealed?"
                		{
                    		tempList -= <<"Why is the temple sealed?">>;
                    		bark("Full of questions, you are. Too much for
                        		my mind, it is.");
                    		bark("Tend to our crops, I must. Time for this,
                        		I have not! To Ezrekal, go. Speak to the
                        		gods, she cannot. So time for you, she will
                        		have.");

                    		tempList ^= <<"Who is Ezrekal?",
                                		"Why can't she speak to the gods?">>;
                		}

						if tempKey = "Who is Ezrekal?"
						{
    						tempList -= <<"Who is Ezrekal?",
                						"Why can't she speak to the gods?">>;
    						bark("Crazy she is, like you.");
    						bark("South and east of here, find her, you
        						will. Away from me. Away from us all.");
    						bark("Go now! In peace, leave me.");

    						exitConvo();
    						return;
						}

						if tempKey = "Why can't she speak to the gods?"
						{
    						tempList -= <<"Who is Ezrekal?",
                						"Why can't she speak to the gods?">>;
    						bark("Crazy she is, like you.");
    						bark("South and east of here, find her, you
        						will. Away from me. Away from us all.");
    						bark("Go now! In peace, leave me.");

    						exitConvo();
    						return;
						}

                		if tempKey = "What are the shades?"
                		{
                    		tempList -= <<"What are the shades?">>;
                    		bark("The spirits of the dead, they are. Nothing,
                        		know you? Look after us and protect us, they
                        		do. Think that simply fade away, they do?");
                    		bark("Stay away from the children, you should.
                        		That your ignorance may spread, afraid, I am.");
                		}

                		if tempKey = "Why don't you honor your ancestors?"
                		{
                    		tempList -= <<"Why don't you honor your ancestors?">>;
                    		bark("Insult me, you do! Deaf, are you?");
                    		bark("Honor the shades, we do. Go to the Sacred
                        		Circle, we do not.");

                    		tempList ^= <<"What is the Sacred Circle?",
                                		"Why don't you go there?">>;
                		}

                		if tempKey = "What is the Sacred Circle?"
                		{
                    		tempList -= <<"What is the Sacred Circle?">>;
                    		bark("Where we feel the shades gather, it is.");
                    		bark("On the rock promintory, just north of here,
                        		it is. Both the temple and the Vale, it
                        		overlooks.");
                		}

                		if tempKey = "Why don't you go there?"
                		{
                    		tempList -= <<"Why don't you go there?">>;
                    		bark("Filled with sadness, now it is. Once
                        		whispers from lost loved ones, there,
                        		we heard. Only laments, hear now, we do.
                        		Dying, our land is. And with it, our
                        		people.");
                    		bark("Gone, the gods are. From them, find
								comfort, we will not. So go there, we
								do not.");
                		}

                		if tempKey = "Why has everything changed?"
                		{
                    		tempList -= <<"Why has everything changed?">>;
                    		bark("Addled, your wits are! Know you nothing?!");
                    		bark("You Elder, who is? Unforgivable, it is, in
                        		such ignorance to let you walk around. A bad
                        		example for the children, it is.");
                    		bark("Your first tales, learn, you must. And time
                        		for it, I have not. Back to your Elder, go.
                        		Her duty, it is, not mine.");
                		}
					}

        			if tempKey = "Why are they angry?"
        			{
            			tempList -= <<"Why are they angry?">>;
            			bark("Unable to stop the Titans, we were. Rather than
                			fight, ran, many did. Against beings who battle
							gods, what use are we?");
            			bark("But defend them, we did not. Failed them, we did.
                			Speak to us, they will not.");

            			tempList ^= <<"Stop the Titans?",
                        			"Beings who battle gods?">>;

						tempKey = ask(tempList);

        				if tempKey = "Stop the Titans?"
        				{
            				tempList -= <<"Stop the Titans?">>;
            				bark("Better you could do, I suppose? Ha!");
            				bark("Seen the Vale, you have. Cut off from the rest of
                				the world, once we were not. But sealed us here,
                				they did. And sealed the temple, too.");
            				bark("Better that died, we all should have, than without
                				the gods to live.");
        				}

        				if tempKey = "Beings who battle gods?"
        				{
            				tempList -= <<"Beings who battle gods?">>;
            				bark("Zealans, the proper order, know. Life to us, the
                				gods give. All things good, from them, flow. To
                				them, prayers and offerings, we give.");
            				bark("If life, the gods give, life, take away, they
                				can. Stupid enough to contend with the gods, who
                				is? Not Zealans. But battle them, the Titans did.
                				If strong enough to fight gods, strong enough to
                				crush the Zealans, they were. Do what, could we?");
        				}
					}

					answer = ask(askList);
				}

        		if tempKey = "Why is your history tragic?"
        		{
           			tempList-= <<"Why is your history tragic?">>;
           			bark("Long ago, before born, my great-grandmother was,
						peace in the Vale, there was. Flowing water, there
						was, and everywhere, green plants.");
					bark("But shattered, the happiness was, when Gunnar - a
						child from the other tribe - killed Hoskuld. Hoskuld,
						my kin was. From that day forth, blood feud between
						our clans, has been.");

					tempKey = ask(tempList);
        		}

				answer = ask(askList);
    		}

   			case "First tales?"
   			{
  				askList -= <<"First tales?">>;

    			if not zealanMark
    			{
	     			bark("Tell an outsider, I should? Think me addled, you
						must! For OUR children, the tales are. Not for
						children of Pagans!");
    			}
    			else
    			{
	     			bark("To teach you, too late it is. Other gods, know, you
						do. Skeptical as any grown Zealan, you are. Feel the
						magic touch your heart, you cannot. For you, seem as
						silly stories, they would. No, sorry, I am. Tell you,
						I will not.");
   				}
  			}

   			case "Tell me about the other people."
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Tell me about the other people.">>;
				toldOthersConvo();
    		}

   			case "What is it you do?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"What is it you do?">>;

    			if thordisJob
    			{
        			bark("Forgotten, already you have?");
    			}

    			bark("Clan Elder, I am. As before me, of my family, all
        			the women have been.");

				if (thordisJob = false) and (saidWomen = false)
				{
    				askList ^= <<"Elder?", "All the women?">>;
				}
				else if (thordisJob = true) and (saidWomen = false)
				{
    				askList ^= <<"All the women?">>;
				}
				else
				{
    				askList ^= <<"Elder?">>;
				}
   			}

   			case "What is this place?"
   			{
        		askList -= <<"What is this place?">>;
        		bark("Home of the Hrodny's, it is. Ours, always this
            		water has been. Keep it safe, we do, from those
            		dung-beetle Gunnar's.");

        		if thordisMet
        		{
            		bark("Convinced, still I am not, spy of those
                		coward Gunnar's, you are not.");
        		}
        		else
        		{
            		bark("Know you, I do not. How, know I, spy of
                		those coward Gunnar's, you are not?");
        		}
   			}

   			case "Can you direct me to the Test?"
   			{
        		askList -= <<"Can you direct me to the Test?">>;
        		bark("About the Rite of Passage, how do you, an
					outsider, know? For Zealans only, it is!");

        		askList ^= <<"Atli told me of the Test.">>;
   			}

			case "Atli told me of the Test."
			{
				askList -= <<"Atli told me of the Test.">>;
				bark("He did, did he?! That whimpering bag of bloated
					Torax guts! No right, he had, such a thing to tell.
					But always, lower standards, the Gunnar's had.");
				bark("If told you about the Rite, he did, why here, are
					you? Why at the Rite, are you not?");

				askList ^= <<"I wanted more information.",
							"I came seeking your wisdom.">>;
			}

			case "I wanted more information."
			{
				askList ^= <<"I wanted more information.">>;
				bark("Information, HA! Need information, you do not,
					little man. Life, be lived, it must. For yourself,
					do it, you must. If know about the Rite, you do,
					know everything you need to know, you do.");

				if gunnarSpokeStone
				{
					askList ^= <<"Do you have the Passage Stone?">>;
				}
				else
				{
					bark("Now, away, go, if too coward to take the
						Rite, you are!");

					exitConvo();
					return;
				}
			}

			case "I came seeking your wisdom."
			{
				askList ^= <<"I came seeking your wisdom.">>;
				bark("Misjudged you, perhaps I have. Need wisdom, you do.
					Life, painful is. But be lived, it must. For yourself,
					do it, you must. Do it for you, no others can.");

				if gunnarSpokeStone
				{
					askList ^= <<"Do you have the Passage Stone?">>;
				}
				else
				{
					bark("Now, away, go. Face the Rite alone, you must.
						Help you further, I cannot.");

					exitConvo();
					return;
				}
			}

   			case "Tell me of the Test."
   			{
        		askList -= <<"Tell me of the Test.">>;
        		bark("To tell, what is? Rite of Passage, it is. Proves,
            		worthy of being a Zealan, you are. Strong enough,
					you are not.");

        		askList ^= <<"I will take your Test.", "Not strong enough?">>;
   			}

			case "I will take your Test."
			{
        		askList -= <<"I will take your Test.">>;
				bark("Sure of yourself, you are. Fear failure and death,
					do you not?");

				askList ^= <<"Yes.", "No.">>;
			}

			case "Yes."
			{
				askList -= <<"Yes.", "No.">>;
				bark("Good, then survive it, you may. Without fear, only a
					fool lives. Many things, Zealans are. But fools, we are
					not. To the Rite, go you must. Speak further with you,
					I cannot.");

				exitConvo();
				return;
			}

			case "No."
			{
				askList -= <<"Yes.", "No.">>;
				bark("Then survive it, you will not. Without fear, only a
					fool lives. Many things, Zealans are. But fools, we are
					not. To the Rite, go you must. Speak further with you,
					I will not. If live you do, surprised will I be.");

				exitConvo();
				return;
			}
			case "Not strong enough?"
			{
        		askList ^= <<"Not strong enough?">>;
				bark("Famine and war, survived we have. Strong, Zealans are,
					these things to endure. Soft and weak, a Pagan, you are.
					Waste my breath, or the food of my clan, upon you, I
					will not. The Rite, take, if wish it, you do. But without
					the Mark, come back, do not.");

				exitConvo();
				return;
			}

			case "The Gunnar's say you have the Stone."
			{
				askList -= <<"The Gunnar's say you have the Stone.">>;
				bark("And those misbegotten sons of sand worms, belive,
					you do? Lie to the shades of their ancestors, they
					would. The last to have the Stone, the Gunnar's were.
					Lost it, they must have, and place the blame, upon us,
					they wish!");

				hoskuldSpokeStone = true;
			}

			case "Where is the Passage Stone?", "Do you have the Passage Stone?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Where is the Passage Stone?",
							"Do you have the Passage Stone?">>;

				if spokeOnce
				{
					bark("Hit in the head, have you been? Told you once,
						I did. The last to have the Stone, the Gunnar's
						were. Seen it, have we not! If lost it, they have,
						to them, talk. Or perhaps Ragnar, go see. Everywhere,
						he goes. Seen it, maybe he has.");
				}
				else
				{
					bark("Where it is, know, I do not!  The last to have
						the Stone, the Gunnar's were. Seen it, have we not!
						If lost it, they have, their fault, it is. To them,
						go speak.");

					hoskuldSpokeStone = true;
					spokeOnce = true;
				}
			}

   			case "Why will no one speak to me?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Why will no one speak to me?">>;
    			bark("Stranger, you are, an outsider. Trust you, we do not.
					Know how to deal with you, we do not. If Zealan, you
					were, understand you, we might. If Zealan, you were,
					a common background, share, we could.");

    			askList ^= <<"How may I become a Zealan?">>;
   			}

			case "How may I become a Zealan?"
			{
    			askList -= <<"How may I become a Zealan?">>;
				bark("Born to Zealans, be, you must! No other way, there
					is.");

				askList ^= <<"How can I prove myself to you?">>;
			}

			case "How can I prove myself to you?"
			{
				askList -= <<"How can I prove myself to you?">>;
				bark("Prove yourself, wish, I do not. Go away, you would,
					wish, I do. But if go away, you will not, the Rite
					of Passage, take, you must.");
				bark("First, find the Passage Stone, you must. Then to the
					farthest corner of the vale, south and west of here,
					go you must. Made open to you, the way will be, if have
					the Stone, you do. Reach into the Passage Plant, you
					must, and pluck the fruit which, at its heart, grows.");
				bark("The fruit of the Passage Plant, to me, bring. Then
					the Mark, which proclaims you a Zealan, give to you,
					I will.");

				askList ^= <<"Where is the Passage Stone?",
							"That seems too easy.">>;
				thordisToldTest = true;
			}

			case "That seems too easy."
			{
				askList -= <<"That seems too easy.">>;
				bark("True, appearances, rarely are. But the answers to
					life, given, you are not. Figure out the dangers,
					you must. Tell you, I cannot. Now, go, if going,
					you are. Enough time, wasted, I have.");
			}

   			case "How may I be accepted?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"How may I be accepted?">>;
    			bark("Accept you, wish, we do not. Go away, you would,
					wish, I do. Enough food, have, we do not. But if
					go away, you will not, the Rite of Passage, take,
					you must. Only Zealans, within this Vale, may stay.");
				bark("Find the Passage Stone, you must. Then to the
					farthest corner of the vale, south and west of here,
					go. Made open to you, the way will be, if have the
					Stone, you do. Reach into the Passage Plant, you
					must, and pluck the fruit which, at its heart, grows.");
				bark("The fruit of the Passage Plant, to me, bring. Then
					the Mark, which proclaims you a Zealan, give to you,
					I will.");

				askList ^= <<"Where is the Passage Stone?",
							"That seems too easy.">>;
				thordisToldTest = true;
   			}

   			case "Why must I take the Test?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Why must I take the Test?">>;
    			bark("Tradition, it is. All Zealan's, the Rite must
					take. If stay here, you wish, pass the Rite, you
					must. Without the Mark, food and shelter, denied,
					you shall be. Now to the Rite, go, or the Vale,
					leave! Watching you, the shades will be.");
   			}

   			case "What happens if I fail?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"What happens if I fail?">>;
    			bark("If kill you, the Rite does not, driven out of
					the Vale, you shall be. Summon up the shades, we
					shall. Enough food and water, for strangers,
					have, we do not! Go now, you must. Time for this,
					have, I do not.");
   			}

   			case "Where is the Test?"
   			{
    			bark("In the farthest corner of the vale, south and west
					of here, it is. Make haste, you should. Tolerate you
					here for long, the shades will not. Without the
					fruit, come back, do not!");

				exitConvo();
				return;
   			}

   			case "I have returned the shield. Now what?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"I have returned the shield. Now what?">>;
    			bark("Proof, that exist once, the gods did. A legacy
					of our past, it is. But work, it will not, outside
					of the temple. And sealed, the temple is. Speak to
					us, still, the gods, cannot.");

    			askList ^= <<"Why is the temple sealed?",
							"How can I open the temple?">>;
   			}

			case "Why is the temple sealed?"
			{
    			askList ^= <<"Why is the temple sealed?">>;
				bark("Ask me, do not. A Titan, I am not. Sealed, the
					temple was, when war with the Ancient Ones the
					Titans did. Why, I know not.");
			}

			case "How can I open the temple?"
			{
    			askList ^= <<"How can I open the temple?">>;
				bark("An Elder, I am. A farmer too, I am. About stones
					or spells, know nothing, I do. Speak to Hrodny or
					Ezrekal, I would, if you, I were.");

				askList ^= <<"Why Hrodny?", "Why Ezrekal?">>;
			}

			case "Why Hrodny?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Why Hrodny?">>;
				bark("Good with tools, she is. About stones and
					Such, she knows. Think of something to help
					you, she might.");
			}

			case "Why Ezrekal?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Why Ezrekal?">>;
				bark("High Priestess, she is. Hers, the legacy of the
					gods is. Have some devine idea, she might. About
					such things, know, I do not. Only a guess, it is.
					Try it, if interested, you are.");
			}

   			case "How do I free the gods?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"How do I free the gods?">>;
    			bark("Priestess, I am not. Better to ask Ezrekal, you
					should.");
   			}

   			case "What will happen now?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"What will happen now?">>;
    			bark("Once again, a question that, answer I cannot, this
					is. What I hope, tell you, I can. Fertile, our valley
					will be, hope, I do. Return, the game shall, hope, I
					do. In peace, live, we shall, hope, I do. Honor you
					all the days of our lives, we shall. Promise you this,
					I do. Welcome to stay, you are. Our good fortune,
					share with you, gladly we would.");
   			}

   			case "Help me, I've been poisoned."
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Help me, I've been poisoned.",
							"The Test was impossible!">>;
    			bark("About the Rite of Passage, how do you, an
					outsider, know? For Zealans only, it is! Told
					you, that rotting pile of fish offal, Atli did!
					No right, he had, such a thing to tell.");
				bark("But if told you about the Rite, he did, why
					here, are you? Why to him, cry, you do not?
					Poisoned you, he has. No cure for the Passage
					spore, now there is.");

				askList ^= <<"Poisoned?", "No cure?">>;
   			}

			case "Poisoned?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Poisoned?">>;

				if testFromAtli
				{
					bark("Poison, the Passage Plant is. Survive it, no
						one can. Back to Atli, go I would. Kill him, you
						should.");
				}
				else
				{
					bark("Poison, the Passage Plant is. Survive it, no
						one can. Cruel, I was, know, I do. But outsiders
						feed, we cannot. Stay, you could not. And go,
						make you, I could not. Sorry, I am.");
				}

				askList ^= <<"How long will I live?">>;
			}

			case "How long will I live?"
			{
				askList -= <<"How long will I live?">>;

				if not haveMark
				{
					bark("Know, I do not. But to Atli go, and the Mark, get.
						Owes it to you, he does. Make him explain, I would.");

					exitConvo();
					return;
				}
				else
				{
					bark("Know, only Ezrekal, might. But your hopes, get
						up, do not. Useless, she is. But some knowledge,
						have, she might. To her, go. Help you, I cannot.");

					askList ^= <<"Where is Ezrekal?">>;
				}
			}

			case "Where is Ezrekal?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Where is Ezrekal?">>;
				bark("East from here, she lives. Far away, on the other
					side of the vale, find her, you will");

				exitConvo();
				return;
			}

			case "No cure?"
			{
				askList -= <<"No cure?">>;
				bark("Help you now, only the gods can. To the High
					Priestess, go, you could, if the Mark you had. To
					Atli go, and the Mark, get. About these things,
					know, Ezrekal might.");

				askList ^= <<"Where is Ezrekal?">>;
			}

   			case "The Test was impossible!"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Help me, I've been poisoned.",
							"The Test was impossible!">>;
				bark("Taken the Rite of Passage, you, an outsider,
					have? For Zealans only, it is! Told you, that
					rotting pile of fish offal, Atli did! No right,
					he had, such a thing to tell.");
				bark("But if told you about the Rite, he did, why
					here, are you? Why to him, cry, you do not?
					Poisoned you, he has. No cure for the Passage
					spore, now there is.");

				askList ^= <<"Poisoned?", "No cure?">>;
   			}

   			case "I have taken your Test.", "The plant exploded!", "What is happening to me?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"I have taken your Test.",
							"The plant exploded!",
							"What is happening to me?">>;
    			bark("Survive,  you would, think, I did not. Or
					warned you, I would have. Poisoned, you have
					been. Sorry, I am. No cure, there is. My
					people, protect, I must. Here, the Mark, is.
					Comfortable, make you, we will. Owe you
					that much, I do.");

// ADD GIVE ZEALAN MARK TO PLAYER
    			zealanMark = true;
				askList ^= <<"Poisoned?", "No cure?">>;
   			}

   			case "Can you heal me?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Can you heal me?">>;
    			bark("ME? Of course not. The poison, only the High
					Priestess could... before stop speaking to us,
					the gods did. Now, fatal, the poison is. Now,
					the hopelessness of the Zealans, you know. Go
					to Ezrekal, you could. But do nothing for you,
					she will.");

    			askList ^= <<"Where is Ezrekal?">>;
   			}

   			case "Ezrekal can do nothing!"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Ezrekal can do nothing!">>;
    			bark("Surprises you, this does? Told you as much, I
					did. Be resigned to your fate, you should. Much
					trouble, it saves. The Cloud Cliffs, climb, you
					could. And the gods, yourself ask. If tired of
					living, already you are.");

    			askList ^= <<"Cloud Cliffs?", "Where are the Cloud Cliffs?">>;
   			}

   			case "Is there no hope for me?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Is there no hope for me?">>;
    			bark("The poison, only the High Priestess could...
					before stop speaking to us, the gods did. Now,
					fatal, the poison is. Now, the hopelessness of
					the Zealans, you know. Go to Ezrekal, you can.
					But do nothing for you, she will.");

    			askList ^= <<"Where is Ezrekal?">>;
   			}

   			case "Tell me more of the cliffs."
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Tell me more of the cliffs.">>;
    			bark("Nothing more to tell, there is. South they are,
					from here. Cross the liquid fire to them, get, you
					must. Only one who, the cliff key holds, safely
					pass, can.");

				askList ^= <<"Where is the cliff key?">>;
   			}

			case "What happened to Tyorvi?"
			{
				askList -= <<"What happened to Tyorvi?">>;
				bark("Poisoned by Ingyald's brews, his mind was. Speak
					to the gods, he sought. Tell them, starving, we are
					he would. Up at night, two of them, went. By morning,
					dead, Tyorvi's friend was, and mad, Tyorvi was.");

    			askList ^= <<"Tyorvi's friend?", "Mad?">>;
			}

			case "Tyorvi's friend?"
			{
				 askList -= <<"Tyorvi's friend?">>;
				 bark("Drunken fool, he was. Talked Tyorvi into it, he
				 	did. Getting Tyorvi into trouble, always, he was.
					But like a brother, him, Tyorvi loved. Do what, a
					sister can? From Ingyald, said stay away, I did.
					But listen, Tyorvi would not. Now dead, Tyorvi's
					friend is. And useless, my brother is.");
			}

			case "Mad?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Mad?">>;
				bark("Blames himself, Tyorvi does. Says, died, he should
					have, instead of his friend. Climb the cliffs, he
					would, if watch him, I did not. Says have the cliff
					key, he does not. Believe him, I do not. But do
					nothing, I can... except from Ingyald's brews, him keep.");

				askList ^= <<"Where is the cliff key?">>;
			}

   			case "Has no one climbed the cliffs before?"
   			{
    			askList -= <<"Has no one climbed the cliffs before?">>;
    			bark("Idiots and men driven mad by Ingyald's poison.
					Those crazy enough to listen to crazy old Ezrekal.
					Climb the Cloud Cliffs, you should. Find the gods,
					you can. And found the gods, they have. Dead! All
					of them, dead, they are!");

    			askList ^= <<"Cloud Cliffs?">>;
   			}

			case "Cloud Cliffs?"
			{
    			askList -= <<"Cloud Cliffs?">>;
				bark("The gateway to the Cloud City, they are. No
					wonder, die, all the fools who tro to climb, do.
					The gods' doorstep, it is.");

				askList ^= <<"Where are the Cloud Cliffs?",
							"Gods' doorstep?">>;
			}

			case "Where are the Cloud Cliffs?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Where are the Cloud Cliffs?">>;
				bark("South they are, from here. Cross the liquid fire
					to them, get, you must. Only one who, the cliff
					key holds, safely pass, can.");

				askList ^= <<"Where is the cliff key?">>;
			}

			case "Where is the cliff key?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Where is the cliff key?">>;

				if toldAboutAddiction
				{
					bark("Know, I do not. Tyorvi, the last one to
						hold it was. Ask him, you can. Maybe even
						answer you, he will. Like to talk about it,
						he does not.");
				}
				else
				{
					bark("Know, I do not. Ask someone else, you must.");
				}
			}

			case "Gods' doorstep?"
			{
				askList -= <<"Gods' doorstep?">>;
				bark("At the top of the cliffs, find the Cloud City,
					you will, or so the legends say. The home of the
					Ancient Ones, the Cloud City is. A place of
					beauty, said to be, it is. Forbidden to mortals,
					it is.");

				cloudCity = true;
			}

			case ""
			{
				bark("Waste my time, you do! When something to say,
					you have, return. Until then, away, go!");

				exitConvo();
				return;
			}

			case"bye"
			{
				ran = urandom(4);

				if ran = 1
				{
					bark("Until our shades meet.");
				}
				if ran = 2
				{
					bark("Farewell.");
				}
				if ran = 3
				{
					bark("Goodbye.");
				}

				exitConvo();
				return;
			}
		}
	}
}


process Thordis::toldOthersConvo()
{
	[[PT_DEFAULT, referent]];

	reply : Number;
	tempKey : String;
	tempList : String List;

	if (toldMyTribe = false) and (toldOthers = false)
	{
    	bark("My people or the others?");

    	tempList ^= <<"Your people.", "The others.">>;
    	tempKey = ask(tempList);
	}
	else if (toldMyTribe = true) and (toldOthers = false)
	{
        bark("What else, wish you to know?");

    	tempList ^= <<"The others.">>;
    	tempKey = ask(tempList);
	}
	else if (toldMyTribe = false) and (toldOthers = true)
	{
        bark("What else, wish you to know?");

    	tempList ^= <<"Your people.">>;
    	tempKey = ask(tempList);
	}
	else
	{
      	bark("Told you of everyone, I have.
			No others, there are.");
		bark("Tell you again of them, I should?");

		reply = askYesNo();

		if reply = true
		{
    		bark("My people or the others?");

			toldMyTribe = false;
			toldOthers = false;
			toldSelf = false;
			toldTyorvi = false;
			toldRagnar = false;
			toldAtli = false;
			toldHrodny = false;
			toldIngyald = false;
			toldEzrekal = false;

    		tempList ^= <<"Your people.", "The others.">>;
    		tempKey = ask(tempList);
		}
		else
		{
    		bark("Make up your mind, you should.");
		}
	}

    if tempKey = "Your people."
    {
      	tempList -= <<"Your people.">>;
      	bark("Of me, Tyorvi, or Ragnar, wish you to know?");

       	if not toldSelf
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"You">>;
       	}

       	if not toldTyorvi
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Tyorvi">>;
       	}

       	if not toldRagnar
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ragnar">>;
       	}

		if (toldSelf = true) and (toldTyorvi = true)
			and (toldRagnar = true)
		{
	       	toldMyTribe = true;
		}

    	tempKey = ask(tempList);
    }

    if tempKey = "The others."
    {
      	tempList -= <<"The others.">>;
      	bark("Of Atli, Ingyald, Hrodny or Ezrekal, wish you to know?");

       	if not toldAtli
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Atli">>;
       	}

       	if not toldIngyald
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ingyald">>;
       	}

       	if not toldHrodny
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Hrodny">>;
       	}

       	if not toldEzrekal
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ezrekal">>;
       	}

		if (toldAtli = true) and (toldHrodny = true)
			and (toldIngyald = true) and (toldEzrekal = true)
		{
	       	toldOthers = true;
   		}

    	tempKey = ask(tempList);
    }

    if tempKey = "You"
    {
	    tempList -= <<"You">>;
        bark("Nothing to tell, there is. Clan Elder, I am. To Tyorvi,
            sister, I am.");
        bark("Mate and children, none, I have. Duty to my people
            only, I have.");

	    toldSelf = true;

		if (toldTyorvi = true) and (toldRagnar = true)
		{
	       	toldMyTribe = true;
		}

       	if not toldTyorvi
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Tyorvi">>;
       	}

       	if not toldRagnar
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ragnar">>;
       	}

    	if toldMyTribe = false
    	{
    		tempKey = ask(tempList);
    	}
    }

    if tempKey = "Tyorvi"
    {
      	tempList -= <<"Tyorvi">>;
      	bark("My younger brother, he is. Care for him, I must, until a
        	mate of his own, he has. But slim chance for that, he has.
        	Few women, there are. A fine husband, make, he would, if any
        	single women you know.");

    	toldTyorvi = true;

		if (toldSelf = true) and (toldRagnar = true)
		{
	       	toldMyTribe = true;
		}

       	if not toldSelf
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"You">>;
       	}

       	if not toldRagnar
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ragnar">>;
       	}

    	if toldMyTribe = false
    	{
    		tempKey = ask(tempList);
    	}
    }

    if tempKey = "Ragnar"
    {
      	tempList -= <<"Ragnar">>;
      	bark("Our hunter, Ragnar is. Brings back fresh meat, he does.
        	Gone, he is, for days at a time. Little game left, there
        	is. Starve soon, we all will, I fear.");

      	toldRagnar = true;

		if (toldSelf = true) and (toldTyorvi = true)
		{
	       	toldMyTribe = true;
		}

       	if not toldSelf
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"You">>;
       	}

       	if not toldTyorvi
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Tyorvi">>;
       	}

    	if toldMyTribe = false
    	{
    		tempKey = ask(tempList);
    	}
    }

    if tempKey = "Atli"
    {
      	tempList -= <<"Atli">>;
      	bark("The leader of the other clan, he is. A pig-headed fool,
        	he is. An in-bred son of carrion flies, he is. Why made him
        	Elder, they did, beyond me, it is. Spine, he has not. Blood
        	of murderers, prosper he shall not!");

      	toldAtli = true;

		if (toldHrodny = true) and (toldIngyald = true)
			and (toldEzrekal = true)
		{
	       	toldOthers = true;
   		}

       	if not toldIngyald
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ingyald">>;
       	}

       	if not toldHrodny
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Hrodny">>;
       	}

       	if not toldEzrekal
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ezrekal">>;
       	}

    	if toldOthers = false
    	{
    		tempKey = ask(tempList);
    	}
    }

    if tempKey = "Ingyald"
    {
      	tempList -= <<"Ingyald">>;
        bark("A truer sign of the gods displeasure, find, you will
            not! Died in childbirth, he should have! Work, he cannot.
            But live on, hardworking men to poison with his foul
            brews, Atli allows.");
        bark("Strangle him myself, I should. And Atli's job, for
            him, do.");

      	toldIngyald = true;

		if (toldAtli = true) and (toldHrodny = true)
			and (toldEzrekal = true)
		{
	       	toldOthers = true;
   		}

       	if not toldAtli
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Atli">>;
       	}

       	if not toldHrodny
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Hrodny">>;
       	}

       	if not toldEzrekal
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ezrekal">>;
       	}

    	if toldOthers = false
    	{
    		tempKey = ask(tempList);
    	}
    }

    if tempKey = "Hrodny"
    {
	    tempList -= <<"Hrodny">>;
        bark("What Atli deserves, she is! Another test from the
            gods, she is. Another test failed, Atli has.");
        bark("Crazy, she is. But stand up to Atli, she does. Grant
            her that, I will. A better Elder, would she be, if
            crazy, she were not.");
        bark("But allow her to speak blasphemy, Atli should not.
            Comdemn us all, her strange ideas do. Of course, exist,
            the gods do! Anger them further, she does. Allow such
            nonsense in my clan, I would not!");

	    toldHrodny = true;

		if (toldAtli = true) and (toldIngyald = true)
			and (toldEzrekal = true)
		{
	       	toldOthers = true;
   		}

       	if not toldAtli
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Atli">>;
       	}

       	if not toldIngyald
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ingyald">>;
       	}

       	if not toldEzrekal
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ezrekal">>;
       	}

    	if toldOthers = false
    	{
    		tempKey = ask(tempList);
    	}
    }

    if tempKey = "Ezrekal"
    {
      	tempList -= <<"Ezrekal">>;
        bark("A good-for nothing, dried up old hag, she is! Sits
            and mutters to herself, she does. Think tithes of food,
            collect, she can. While starve, we do, and speak to
            the gods, she cannot!");
        bark("Sooner such food to Atli, yield, I would! Than on one
            who builds false hope, precious food waste!");

      	toldEzrekal = true;

		if (toldAtli = true) and (toldHrodny = true)
			and (toldIngyald = true)
		{
	       	toldOthers = true;
   		}

       	if not toldAtli
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Atli">>;
       	}

       	if not toldIngyald
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Ingyald">>;
       	}

       	if not toldHrodny
       	{
        	tempList ^= <<"Hrodny">>;
       	}

    	if toldOthers = false
    	{
    		tempKey = ask(tempList);
    	}
	}
}
